Keep shift counts within the width of their operand.

A malformed stream drives several shift counts out of range, which is
undefined behaviour in C++ (UBSan reports):
- trans4m_freq_2_time_fxp.cpp: imdct_fxp() returns an exponent derived
  from the stream's q-format; exp + 15 - SCALING went negative on the
  long-window paths. Every computed shift now goes through
  trans4m_shift(), which clamps it to 0..31.
- ms_synt.cpp: the left/right q-format difference gave shifts up to 51.
- pvmp4audiodecoderframe.cpp: an SBR header left upsamplingFactor at 0, so
  the bit rate was shifted by -1.

